sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant A as API and gate
    participant R as Valkey
    participant G as LangGraph run
    participant D as Domain tier
    participant M as Models (OmniRoute and TEI)
    participant P as PostgreSQL
    C->>A: POST /v1/sessions/{id}/turns with Bearer token and Idempotency-Key
    A->>R: take session lock and rate-limit bucket
    A->>G: invoke the graph for this turn
    G->>P: BEGIN, lock the session row (FOR UPDATE NOWAIT)
    G->>G: load: replay check, kill switches, hydrate if the checkpoint lags
    G->>M: input rails and turn analysis (guard-input and nlu-extract in parallel)
    G->>P: append TURN_INPUT and four GUARD_VERDICT events
    G->>G: route: withdraw, safety, objection, side-query, or the state node
    G->>D: decisions and reference reads (eligibility, suitability, ranking, quotes)
    G->>G: decide: pure fsm.transition, append STATE_TRANSITION
    G->>M: retrieve (embed, search, rerank) and compose (gen-converse or gen-recommend)
    G->>G: validate: output rails and release policy
    G->>P: write conv rows and RESPONSE_RELEASED, then COMMIT (I8)
    G->>R: idempotency hint, publish turn.released
    G-->>A: the released body as canonical JSON bytes
    A-->>C: 200 body, and SSE turn.released
